  "term": "suprarenal gland",
  "definition": "The suprarenal gland, also called the adrenal gland, is a roughly triangular gland that sits on top of each kidney. It is a ductless gland that releases hormones into the body, including epinephrine and norepinephrine from its medulla and steroid hormones from its cortex.",
